title: Veeam: Managed Servers
agents: special
catalog: os/storage
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors a server managed by a Veeam Backup & Replication
 server, collected via the Veeam special agent: a Microsoft Windows or Linux
 server, a VMware vSphere or Cloud Director host, a Hyper-V server or
 cluster, an SCVMM server or an SMB3 server. It reports the server type and
 its status in Veeam, and, in the details, its description and roles.

 The status is Veeam's view of whether the backup server can reach and
 manage this server. "Unavailable" means Veeam cannot reach or manage it,
 for example because the server is down, unreachable over the network, or
 has credential or Veeam component problems.

 This check is {OK} if the server is available to Veeam and {CRIT} if it is
 unavailable. Both states are configurable. Any other status, or no status
 at all, is {UNKNOWN}.

 A server can have two roles: "Backup server" and "Default mount server".
 The backup server itself is a managed server too, and is reported with the
 role "Backup server". A server with neither role is reported with
 "Roles: none".

 The data can be read with the "Veeam Backup Viewer" role.

discovery:
 One service is created for each managed server reported by the API.

item:
 The name of the managed server.
